# What does not belong in the build context. Everything here either makes the
# image bigger or makes it wrong: node_modules of another platform, a dist
# from yesterday, or a .env holding real credentials.
#
# The order matters: the last pattern that matches a path decides. The
# exception for the packages of the foundation comes first, so that the rules
# for node_modules, dist and the rest below still apply inside them. In the
# other order the exception took the node_modules of this machine along, with
# links pointing at C:/, and the build in the image failed for want of the
# types of Node.

# Of the submodule only the packages of the foundation and the root files the
# workspace reads its configuration from. The packages of the
# Handwerkersoftware beside them are no members of this workspace, and its
# documents, scripts and assets are not built here.
upstream/opengewerk/packages/*
!upstream/opengewerk/packages/platform
upstream/opengewerk/docs/
upstream/opengewerk/docker/
upstream/opengewerk/assets/
upstream/opengewerk/*.md
upstream/opengewerk/LICENSE
upstream/opengewerk/Dockerfile

.git/
# The submodule has a file called .git that points into the .git above.
**/.git
.github/
**/.github/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
**/preview-build/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# None of this is built or shipped.
docs/
docker/
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE

# assets/ is shipped: it is the public folder of the interface build
# (publicDir in packages/web/vite.config.ts), so assets/brand is what the image
# serves under /brand. Only the README next to the brand files stays out; it is
# written for people, not for browsers.
assets/brand/README.md
